WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.035
Bladesmiths,
welcome to The Forge.

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:04.403
Eric, it's good to see you.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.738
Good to see you.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:09.242 line:8%
GRADY: Jesse, you've tallied
up a total of $40,000.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:14.213
And if you win out, you stand a
chance at taking home $50,000.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.382
But, Eric, if you
came out on top,

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:18.183
that's your first
Gladiator of the Forge win.

00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:19.786
And you'll get a $5,000 check.

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:21.954
And we'll ask if you wanna come
join us in the final battle

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:23.389
of this competition series.

00:00:23.455 --> 00:00:30.329
You're gonna be building
this, the Acinaces.

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.265
DAVID BAKER (VOICEOVER): The
Acinaces traces its origin

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:35.467
back to the first millennium
BC all across the Mediterranean

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:36.903
region.

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:39.272
This deadly double-edged dagger
was used by Roman gladiators

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:41.507
in pairs, allowing them
to deliver quick slashes

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.411
and deadly strikes upon
opponents inside the walls

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:45.978
of the Colosseum.

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:47.847
This weapon was so
fierce it was even

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.848
believed to have been
wielded by Mithras,

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:51.951
the Persian god of the sun.

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:53.386
Now, along with the
weapon, we have also

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.988
chosen the forge
welding technique

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.956
that we want you both to
use to build your blades.

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.591
Now, if you look in
the pantry, you'll

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:03.395
see we have stacks of 1095 and
15n20 high carbon steel bars.

00:01:03.495 --> 00:01:05.431
We want you to take
that steel and turn it

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:08.334
into at least 100-layer
twisted Damascus billet

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.835
from which you will
make your blades.

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:11.504
So work hard, stay sharp.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.239
Your time starts now.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:15.041
I always have the
tendency to pick too

00:01:15.107 --> 00:01:16.175
much material at the beginning.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.412
So I set four layers
off to the side.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.147
That leaves me with
20 layers, which

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:25.218
means I have to cut and restack
5 pieces to get 100 layers.

00:01:25.284 --> 00:01:27.486
So now that my
billet is drawn out--

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:28.688
Come on.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.490
--I need to get this thing
cut into five pieces.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.824
Jesse's not a big guy.

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:34.627
So I wonder how difficult it's
gonna be for him to actually

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.596
twist this hot steel.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:37.664
OK.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.365
Let's see how well this work.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:40.499
J. NEILSON: Step on the plate.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.901
Stand on those.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.902
You're helping to anchor it
and you got better leverage.

00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:44.904
[bleep] it.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.205
Good enough for me.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.841
I already have my blade
mostly forged to shape,

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:50.810
and I get ready for the quench.

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.244
If this quench
fails, it could send

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:55.481
me home and end my win streak.

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:56.549
Here we go.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.050
Jesse is now in the oil.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:01:59.018
That's great.

00:01:59.084 --> 00:02:00.185
It went perfectly.

00:02:00.252 --> 00:02:01.454
The blade looks great.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.455
There's no cracks.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.722
I heard no pings.

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:05.725
Things have been going
great in this round so far.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:09.228
So now, I need to make an
anthropomorphic handle.

00:02:09.294 --> 00:02:10.696
So I grabbed some mild steel.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:14.234
It'll be a lot lighter in
the end, rather than brass.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.067
OK.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.802
My blade looks menacing.

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:18.905
It looks terrifyingly sharp.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.673
The grind lines are
pretty much perfect.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.775
And then, my handle
is just a person.

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:27.814
[laughs] Sounded great.

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:30.182
ERIC: I'm going
to use 22 pieces,

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:32.885
draw it out, split
it into five pieces,

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:34.387
restack it, and draw it again.

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:37.056
That'll put me at 110 layers.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:39.191
I'm scared that once
I start twisting,

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:42.795
I'm just gonna see layers
start pulling apart.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.963
If this fails, there's
no way I'm gonna come

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:48.534
back to win this challenge.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:49.502
Oh, yeah.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:51.336
Everything on my
steel looks good.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.273
It's time to throw
it in the oil.

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:56.943
J. NEILSON: Oh, there you go.
All right.

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:58.277
GRADY POWELL: We got
two quenched blades.

00:02:58.343 --> 00:02:59.979
Colors in that blade
look pretty good when

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:01.213
you put it in the oil.

00:03:01.313 --> 00:03:03.082
Think I got a good
solid blade here.

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:05.184
Some days I even amaze myself.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.353
My sword, it's
gotten a lot lighter.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.455
And I wanna make sure
I leave that tang

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:12.425
a little on the heavy side
and bring that balance back

00:03:12.491 --> 00:03:14.027
a little closer to the handle.

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:16.563
Now, it's time to get
this handle glued up.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:17.563
It's a little man.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:18.998
He, he, he.

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:21.334
The rest of the time
I have left is devoted

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.969
to sharpening this blade.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.871
I couldn't be happier with the
way this blade's turning out.

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:30.309
GRADY POWELL: 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:32.345
Bladesmiths, put
down your tools.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:34.313
This round is over.

00:03:34.379 --> 00:03:36.950
Bladesmiths, welcome
to our strength test.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:41.320
Today, we have the
Roman Throne Chop.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.222
And since you
didn't get a chance

00:03:43.288 --> 00:03:46.025
to pick the technique
or the weapon,

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.760
you get to choose
who goes first.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:48.828
What?

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.099
- I'll take it.
- All right.

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:54.133
Eric, you wanna go first?

00:03:54.199 --> 00:03:57.002
Let's do it, bud.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:58.705
[grunting]

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:21.326
All right, Eric.

00:04:21.393 --> 00:04:22.662
I gotta, say, good job, man.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:23.796
All right.

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:27.133
First of all, there's no
deflection, deformation.

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:28.100
It came out nice.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.635
Did a good job.

00:04:29.735 --> 00:04:32.338
If we could etch this thing
for like another two hours,

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:34.306
this thing would
be amazing looking.

00:04:34.406 --> 00:04:37.042
But the one complaint
I have is there

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:39.178
is a ton of weight on here.

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:41.447
Controlling that
during chops, it rolled

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.048
over on me a couple times.

00:04:43.115 --> 00:04:45.218
Other than that, good job.

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:46.886
Thank you.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.254
All right, Jesse.
You're up.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.789
You ready to go?

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.189
No.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.592
Well, we're
gonna do it anyway.

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:56.228
JESSE: I can tell that
the purpose of this chair

00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:58.463
is to destroy blades.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:04:59.899
It's been such a long road.

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:02.435
But this-- this could be
the beginning of the end.

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:07.072
I may not be here
for the next battle.

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:08.708
[grunting]

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:29.762
All right, Jesse.

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:30.763
Nice job.

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:32.431
It's nice and light.

00:05:32.497 --> 00:05:34.333
It did a good job on the throne.

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:35.500
The edge is fine.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.870
Everything's still
tight and true.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:38.871
Good job.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:39.972
Thank you.

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:44.643
DOUG MARCAIDA: Gladiators
of the Forge, this is it.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.113
This is the sharpness test.

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:50.716
I'm gonna take your weapons and
try to cut through these ropes.

00:05:50.782 --> 00:05:52.351
Eric, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:05:52.451 --> 00:05:53.385
Let's do it, Doug.

00:05:53.452 --> 00:05:54.620
Let's do it.

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:25.817
Damn.

00:06:25.884 --> 00:06:26.619
Better.

00:06:26.685 --> 00:06:27.653
DOUG MARCAIDA: All right, Eric.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.087
Let's talk about
your sword here.

00:06:29.154 --> 00:06:30.523
You have a sharp edge.

00:06:30.589 --> 00:06:33.059
But there is a
weight to your weapon

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:34.627
that makes it hard
to hold on to.

00:06:34.693 --> 00:06:36.395
It did cut most of the ropes.

00:06:36.495 --> 00:06:40.266
But overall, it will cut.

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:41.233
Jesse, your turn.

00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:42.334
You ready?

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:43.802
- Sure.
- All right.

00:06:43.869 --> 00:06:44.904
Let's do it.

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:55.681
[bleep].

00:07:17.736 --> 00:07:18.737
DOUG MARCAIDA: All right, Jesse.

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:20.806
Let's talk about
your weapon here.

00:07:20.872 --> 00:07:23.375
First up, your edge
cut most of the rope,

00:07:23.475 --> 00:07:25.144
except for the last one.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:27.012 line:14%
But I cut at different angles.

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:30.249 line:14%
So I'll call that on me.

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:31.650
But it is sharp.

00:07:31.717 --> 00:07:34.286
What I love about this
is the balance and weight

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:35.554
you have on your weapon.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:37.590
Overall, it will cut.

00:07:42.661 --> 00:07:44.564
Now, guys, both of your
blades performed extremely well

00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:46.966
during our tests, which makes
for a very difficult decision

00:07:47.032 --> 00:07:49.501
for our judges, because now,
they have to decide which one

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:51.770
of you is taking home
that $5,000 check

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:53.505
and the title of
Gladiator of the Forge.

00:07:53.605 --> 00:07:56.508
Jesse, if you win,
that's seven total wins

00:07:56.608 --> 00:07:59.378
and $45,000 in your pocket.

00:07:59.478 --> 00:08:01.280
Eric, if you came
out on top, that's

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:02.381
your first Gladiator
of the Forge

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:03.949
win in a redemption round.

00:08:04.049 --> 00:08:05.684
And you'll get a
$5,000 check, and we'll

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:07.786
ask if you want to come
join us in the final battle

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:09.255
of this competition series.

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:11.623
Our judges did make
a final decision.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.894
Gentleman, the Gladiator
of the Forge today is--

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:24.336
Jesse, congratulations.

00:08:24.403 --> 00:08:25.804
You did it again, man.

00:08:25.904 --> 00:08:28.073
Eric, it's been an
honor to watch you work.

00:08:28.174 --> 00:08:30.042
But unfortunately, your
blade did not make the cut

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:31.276
by the smallest of margins.

00:08:31.376 --> 00:08:32.711
And J. is gonna tell you why.

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:34.446
J. NEILSON: It basically
just came down to weight.

00:08:34.513 --> 00:08:36.215
There was so much
weight in that handle.

00:08:36.281 --> 00:08:37.616
It made it harder to control.

00:08:37.716 --> 00:08:39.919
And that's the reason
we're sending you home.

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:40.920
I get it.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.054
I get it.

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:44.723
At least I made you guys
work for it this time.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.526 line:8%
Jesse, that is seven
battles and seven victories.

00:08:47.626 --> 00:08:50.162 line:8%
You just won another
check for $5,000.

00:08:50.229 --> 00:08:52.497
Well done.

00:08:52.564 --> 00:08:54.699
You now have $45,000
in your pocket

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:58.170
and you are 7 titles in,
with a chance for one more

00:08:58.236 --> 00:09:00.839
if you have enough in you to
go back in the Forge and battle

00:09:00.906 --> 00:09:01.807
again.

00:09:01.908 --> 00:09:02.974
What do you say?

00:09:03.041 --> 00:09:04.343
Yeah.

00:09:04.443 --> 00:09:05.310
Fantastic.

00:09:05.377 --> 00:09:06.478
I can see the finish line.

00:09:06.545 --> 00:09:08.080
Why not keep going?

00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:09.482
What just happened?

00:09:09.549 --> 00:09:12.084
I'm somehow the seven time
Gladiator of the Forge.

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:13.052
Awesome, man.

00:09:13.152 --> 00:09:14.654
Well, congratulations again.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:16.956
We can't wait to see you battle
it out in the final battle.

00:09:17.023 --> 00:09:17.923
Well done, man.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:18.891
Thank you.

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:21.260
I keep on saying
that this battle is

00:09:21.326 --> 00:09:22.594
closer than my previous battle.

00:09:22.694 --> 00:09:25.397
I can't imagine a
scenario in which it'll

00:09:25.463 --> 00:09:26.832
be closer for the next battle.

00:09:26.898 --> 00:09:30.469
I never expected to be
fighting for the last 5 grand

00:09:30.569 --> 00:09:31.770
to 50 grand.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:35.675
But I'm gonna keep my
place on the throne.

